--- body ---
## Context

[[0926]] showed that each donor publishes in its own way: ADB behind
Cloudflare, with project sheets (Project Data Sheet) updated as disbursements
proceed and agreements published under intermediate pages; itie.sn and aser.sn
failing on certificates; dgMarket behind a login. The system needs a
per-site scraping memory, and periodic tracking of documents that evolve. The
stake (numbering from before 2026-09-29: M2, M3, AEDIST) is to track in near
real time: structured channels (CRS, IATI) arrive with a one-to-three-year lag.

## Author decisions (2026-09-25)

- One memory per site, versioned in the repository, read by the agents and by
  the collector; no `.claude/rules` rule (`paths:` scoping does not
  distinguish sites) and no Claude memory (local to one machine).
- The ontology distinguishes responsible party, publisher and distributor: "on
  reste dans les considérants de gestion documentaire de base" [we stay within
  basic document-management considerations].
- A site file from three documents on.
- Three document classes: frozen, living, series (annual reports,
  quarterly reports…).
- Collection runs on padme; doudou supervises, checks, and defers when SSH does
  not answer. The author lifts checks or logins through a padme screen
  forwarded to doudou.
- Sites' terms of use: delicate subject; always flag, never fail silently.
- Collection methods: `script`, `script-cookies`, `browser-automated`,
  `browser-manual`, `archive-record`, `local-record`.
- Proximity to the event is the first consideration of a judgment, never an
  automatic rank (`docs/jetp-fusion.md` § 5); the lag of structured channels is
  to be measured, not assumed.

## Children

- [[1181]] Document ontology: responsible party, publisher, distributor; series and issues
- [[1182]] Site files: scraping memory per distributor
- [[1183]] Browser driven on padme, collection methods renamed, ADB pilot
- [[1184]] Periodic tracking on padme: living documents and series
- [[1185]] Measure the lag of structured channels against the primary source

## Neighbouring passes (former M2 train, now M3a and M4 since 2026-09-29, tracker [[0715]])

The **pass launcher on padme** belongs to [[1184]]: persistent checkout outside
the author's copy, scheduling, a pass report that flags without blocking,
supervision from doudou, surfacing in `/lair`. Three tickets plug into it
instead of each building their own:

- [[1141]] monthly link check and relaunch of Web Archive captures:
  this is the "frozen documents" pass of [[1184]]. Its machinery exists
  ([[0925]]); it lays down the minimal version of the launcher, which [[1184]]
  takes over and generalises.
- [[1140]] local agent watch: a "discovery" pass, outside the already known
  sites. It reads the site files of [[1182]] and deposits its candidates in the
  same queue as [[1184]] (`_source_watch`), never admitted automatically.
- [[1060]] full test suite after every merge: same launcher pattern and same
  surfacing in `/lair`, but in its own checkout, so that collection diffs never
  mix with tests.

**Storage seam** (author, 2026-09-29): at milestone M4, document storage moves
to a Zotero group library ([[1510]]). The passes of the former M2 (M3a, M4)
therefore write every document or version through the single deposit function
of [[1184]] (action 4), so that M4 changes what is behind it without rewriting
them.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The five children are closed
- [ ] Integration review done (`/roar` step 8): an ADB living document is recollected by the periodic tracking on padme, its site described by its file, its method displayed on the public site
